33[1B- Upper bound: 33 colored edges always force a mono triangle (R(3,3) = 6 + α ≥ n[1B[2Cm argume[11Ct)[0m   [13C[K[1B[2C[38;2;124;124;124mLow[16C2[32Ccan avoid mono[47Ctriangle (explicit construction[79C[0m [79C[K[1B[38;2;124;124;124musing 5-group Ramsey K_5 coloring)[1B[0m                                                                               [K[1B                                 [K[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[38;2;124;124;124mLet[0m[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[3C[38;2;124;124;124m me wr[2B[0m[38;2;135;215;255m⡤⠀[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[9C[38;2;124;124;124mite t[0m[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[14C[38;2;124;124;124mhe pro[0m[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[20C[38;2;124;124;124mof n[2B[0m[38;2;135;215;255m⠤⠄[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[24C[38;2;124;124;124mow.[0m[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[J[38;2;124;124;124mThe structure is clear. Let me summarize:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mGroups: A=(0,1), B=(2,5), C=(3,6), D=(4,7), E=(8,)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mRed group graph edges: A-D, A-E, B-C, B-D, C-E[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mBlue group graph edges: A-B, A-C, B-E, C-D, D-E[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBoth are triangle-free at the group level (5 vertices, 5 edges each, forming [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mC_5).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mRed: A-D-E-C-B-A? A-D, D-B, B-C, C-E, E-A → yes, that's C_5: A-D-B-C-E-A.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mBlue: A-B-E-D-C-A? A-B, B-E, E-D, D-C, C-A → yes, that's C_5: A-B-E-D-C-A.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the red group graph is C_5 and the blue group graph is the complementary C_5![0m[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the classic Ramsey R(3,3) > 5 construction (2-coloring K_5 with two [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcomplementary C_5's, both triangle-free).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the construction is:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Take 5 groups: 4 pairs + 1 singleton = 9 vertices.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. Between groups, use the Ramsey coloring of K_5 (red = one C_5, blue = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcomplementary C_5).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. Within each pair, leave the edge uncolored.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. Between two groups, color ALL 4 (or 2) edges the same color as the group-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlevel edge.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis gives:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Red edges: 5 group-level red edges × 4 edges per pair-pair (or 2 for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msingleton) = A-D(4) + A-E(2) + B-C(4) + B-D(4) + C-E(2) = 16[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Blue edges: A-B(4) + A-C(4) + B-E(2) + C-D(4) + D-E(2) = 16[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Uncolored: 4 (within pairs)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Total colored: 32[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNo monochromatic triangle because:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Within a group: only 2 vertices, no triangle.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Across groups: a monochromatic triangle would need 3 groups forming a mono [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtriangle in the group graph, but both the red and blue group graphs are C_5 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(triangle-free).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Two vertices from one group + one from another: the two vertices in the same [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgroup have the same color to the third vertex, but the edge within the group is [0m[38;2;124;124;124muncolored, so no triangle.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a beautiful construction![0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow for the upper bound:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mClaim: Any coloring of 33 edges (3 uncolored) forces a monochromatic triangle.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof: The 3 uncolored edges form a graph H on 9 vertices with 3 edges. By [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mGallai's theorem (α + τ = n), and τ ≤ m = 3, we get α(H) ≥ 9 - 3 = 6. So there [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mexist 6 vertices with no uncolored edge among them. All C(6,2) = 15 edges among [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthose 6 vertices are colored (red or blue). By R(3,3) = 6, there exists a [0m
